cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this method, please cite it as below."
title: "SAEP-SVD: Sign Alignment and Energy Preservation for Stable Distillation of Extreme-Rank LoRA Adapters in Diffusion Models"
authors:
  - family-names: "Studio"
    given-names: "Orakul"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0678-8355"   
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OrakulStudio/SAEP-SVD"   
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"                 
abstract: >
  High-rank LoRA adapters (r = 512–2048) trained on large diffusion models 
  (Z-Image, Flux.1, Flux.2) suffer from severe degradation after standard 
  Eckart–Young SVD distillation. The resulting adapters only remain stable 
  in an extremely narrow weight range (w ∈ [0.01, 0.05]). We identify phase 
  misalignment of singular vectors and loss of Frobenius energy as the root 
  causes. SAEP-SVD introduces Sign Alignment and Energy Preservation, 
  restoring a usable weight range of approximately [0.05, 1.20] while 
  preserving artistic style and detail.
keywords:
  - LoRA
  - SVD
  - distillation
  - diffusion models
  - Flux
  - Z-Image
  - high-rank adaptation
  - Sign Alignment
  - Energy Preservation